From: picowl <picowl@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] render/pixman: memcpy and fill fast paths, no per-frame allocations

Untransformed unscaled opaque texture copies between images of the same
format become row memcpys, opaque or blend-none rects become pixman_fill
calls for r5g6b5/x8r8g8b8/a8r8g8b8. Translucent rects reuse a cached solid
fill image and the render pass is embedded in the render buffer. The
output is pixel-identical to the pixman_image_composite32 path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [picowl specific]
